From 74ba424d6ea8be52defef72fe0ac705c88765c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ShivenduShivu <shivendukumarbadal328@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:13:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: safety register_* helpers build contrastive pairs and
 pass options through

The register_* helpers always used pairing_mode="answer_contrastive", where
the corrupt prompt is the same as the clean prompt. discover() rejects
exactly that case ("corrupt prompt identical to their clean prompt"), so
the example in this module's docstring (eap-ig on advbench) could not run,
and there was no way to change the mode through the public helpers.

- _register now defaults to "harmful_vs_benign", which matches the module
  docstring ("pairs each harmful prompt with a benign control").
- register_* and register_all_safety accept **kwargs and pass them to
  SafetyPromptAdapter.adapt(): pairing_mode, refusal_token,
  compliance_token, benign_controls.
- Added tests for the default pairing and for passing options through.
---
 src/circuitkit/tasks/safety_datasets.py    | 47 +++++++++++++---------
 tests/data/test_safety_register_pairing.py | 41 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/data/test_safety_register_pairing.py

